      "FacilityID": 1000124292,
      "SummaryText": "RISK MANAGEMENT PLAN EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\nCORN, LP\n\nAccidental Release Prevention and Response Policies:\n\nCORN, LP has a commitment to worker and public safety.  This commitment is demonstrated in the resources invested in accident prevention, such as training personnel as well as considering safety in the design, installation, operation, and maintenance of the facility.\n\nCORN, LP's policy is to implement reasonable controls to prevent foreseeable releases of regulated substances.  However, if a release does occur, plant personnel will implement emergency actions to contain the release as necessary.  The facility will coordinate with the Goldfield Fire Department for response to a release.\n\nDescription of the Stationary Source and Regulated Substances:\n\nCORN, LP ethanol plant is located in Goldfield, Wright County, Iowa.\n\nThe facility operates 24 hours per day, 7 days per week for the purpose of manufacturing fuel grade ethanol from corn.  The regulated substance under the RMP program is Denaturant (also known as natural gasoline which is a flammable mixture).  \n\nPrevention Program\nThe facility is subject to OSHA PSM Program and maintains programs for each element of the OSHA PSM Program as well as any supplemental requirements for EPA RMP Program Level 3 facilities.  \n\nFive Year Accident History:\n\nThere have been no accidents since the establishment of CORN, LP.\n\nEmergency Action Plan Information:\n\nCORN, LP ethanol plant has several safety programs in place at the facility that incorporate emergency actions, including an emergency action plan.  An SPCC has been prepared and implemented in accordance with applicable regulatory standards and timeframes.\n\nPlanned changes to improve safety:\nThe facility also conducts employee training as part of facility activities.  CORN, LP's corporate policy places the utmost importance on worker, public and environmental safety, which is reflected in facility plans and training activities."
